  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Lo, la, los, las",
   "texto": [
    "In a main affirmative sentence, the object pronoun usually goes **detrás** of the verb, attached with script: **Vi o filme** → **Vi-o** (I saw it), **Comprei-a** (I bought it).",
    "It is an initial pattern for European Portuguese; the position also depends on the type of prayer and the words that introduce it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "When he goes in front",
   "texto": [
    "In frequent contexts of proclysis, such as after **não**, **nunca** or **que**, the pronoun goes before the verb and without script: **Não o vi**, **Nunca a comprei**, **Disse que o viu**.",
    "**Também o vi** (I also saw it) is another common example. Don't take a single pattern as a rule for all sentences."
   ]
  },
